<title>UK: LIFFE white sugar holds tight range to quiet close.</title>
<headline>LIFFE white sugar holds tight range to quiet close.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>White sugar futures trading remained subdued up to the close with traders still looking for fresh fundamental news to shake the market from its tight trading range.</p>
<p>The March contract ended at $303.10 a tonne, up $0.90 from Friday, with other positions mixed. Turnover was 1,218 lots.</p>
<p>Paris white sugar ended with March at $303.00, unchanged from Friday.</p>
<p>London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7771</p>
